      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While your story can certainly utilize rich, dark imagery, framing a cultural group as \"primitive\" or \"untamed\" compared to \"civilized\" protagonists risks perpetuating harmful stereotypes that undermine the antagonist's complex motivation. A more compelling and respectful approach would be to explore what your villainic society values differently, perhaps prioritizing tradition, harsh survival, or a rigid philosophical code that clashes with your protagonists' methods rather than labeling them as \"less developed.\" This shifts the conflict from one of inherent superiority to a clash of worldviews, making the villain feel truly threatening and fascinating without relying on offensive archetypes.",
